"Internal Error ()\nciteturn2view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.cochise.az.gov/220/Geographic-Information-Systems\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: URL https://www.cochise.az.gov/220/Geographic-Information-Systems is not safe to open (non-retryable error)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPlanning & Zoning Division | Cochise County, AZ (https://cochise.az.gov/231/Planning-Zoning-Division)\nciteturn2view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://cochise.az.gov/231/Planning-Zoning-Division\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 155\nL0: ###\nL1: \nL2: cite0†Skip to Main Content L3: \nL4: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL5: \nL6: cite1†Create a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nL7: \nL8:   * cite2†Website Sign In L9: \nL10: [Input][Input]\nL11: \nL12: [Input: Search...] Search\nL13: \nL14:   1. cite3†Home L15:   2. cite4†Departments L16:   3. cite5†Development Services L17:   4. Planning & Zoning Division\nL18: \nL19: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL20: \nL21: # Planning & Zoning Division\nL22: \nL23: cite6†Image: Sierra Vista L24: ## Welcome to the Planning & Zoning Division of Development Services, Cochise County\nL25: \nL26: We help residents, property owners, and applicants in unincorporated Cochise County (outside city limits) understand zoning requirements and complete planning applications such as special uses, rezonings, minor land divisions, subdivisions, home occupations, and variances. We also maintain and update the Cochise County Comprehensive Plan and related area plans.\nL27: ### WHERE TO BEGIN\nL28: \nL29:   * Check the zoning of a property (Interactive Zoning Map) – cite7†[Link]†cochise.maps.arcgis.com L30:   * Gather: parcel number (APN) and/or property address\nL31:   * Apply online (Citizenserve Portal) – cite8†[Link]†www4.citizenserve.com L32:   * Request a Zoning Verification Letter – cite9†[Link]†www.cochise.az.gov L33: ### WHAT TYPE OF APPROVAL DO I NEED?\nL34:   * My proposed use is listed as “Permitted” in my zoning districtcite10† (link)†cochisecounty.municipalcodeonline.com L35: → Permitted by Right - you may still need a building permit cite11†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L36:   * My proposed use is listed as “Special Use” in my zoning district cite10† (link)†cochisecounty.municipalcodeonline.com L37: → Special Use Authorization cite12†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L38:   * I want to do something not allowed in my zoning district cite10†(link)†cochisecounty.municipalcodeonline.com L39: → Rezoning cite13†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L40:   * I need relief from a zoning standard (setback, height, lot coverage, etc.)\nL41: → Variance cite14†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L42:   * I disagree with a zoning decision or administrative decision\nL43: → Appeal of a Decision of the Zoning Administrator cite14†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L44:   * I want to split land or create new parcels\nL45: → Minor Land Division (5 or fewer parcels) cite15†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L46: → Subdivision Review (6 or more parcels) cite16†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L47: Not sure which process applies? Contact Planning & Zoning staff before submitting an application.\nL48: ### HOW APPLICATIONS ARE REVIEWED\nL49: \nL50: Planning applications fall into two categories: staff-reviewed (administrative) applications, and applications that require review by a board/commission and may involve a public hearing.\nL51: Administrative Applications (Reviewed and Approved by Development Services Staff)\nL52: These applications are reviewed and approved by staff. Each application will be approved, denied, or approved with conditions. Applicants will be notified in writing by email once a decision is made. Administrative applications include:\nL53:   * Accessory Dwelling Unit (ADU) cite17†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L54:   * Agricultural Zoning Exemption cite18†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L55:   * Home Occupation cite19†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L56:   * Lot Modification cite20†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L57:   * Minor Land Division cite15†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L58:   * Special Event cite21†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L59:   * Special Use Modification (Minor - Administrative) cite12†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L60:   * Zoning Verification Letter cite22†(PDF) L61: Non-Administrative Applications (Reviewed and Approved by Board or Commission, Requires a Public Hearing)\nL62: Non-Administrative applications require review by staff and review/approval by the Planning and Zoning Commission, Board of Adjustment, and/or Board of Supervisors. A cite23†pre-application meeting†www.cochise.az.gov is required before submitting any of the applications listed below. Meetings are complimentary and may be conducted in person or virtually. Applicants should request a meeting date at least four (4) weeks before applying through the portal. Non-administrative applications include:\nL63:   * Comprehensive Plan Amendment cite24†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L64:   * Master Development Plan cite25†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L65:   * Rezoning cite13†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L66:   * Special Use cite12†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L67:   * Special Use Appeal cite12†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L68:   * Special Use Modification (Non-Administrative) cite12†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L69:   * Subdivision Plat cite16†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L70:   * Variance cite14†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L71:   * Zoning Decision Appeal cite14†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L72:   * Zoning Text Amendment cite26†(link)†www.cochise.az.gov L73: ### ZONING\nL74: Zoning guides land development according to the County's Comprehensive Plan and helps protect public health, safety, and welfare. Each zoning district sets allowed land uses, minimum lot sizes, and site standards such as setbacks and screening. You can check a property's zoning using the County's interactive zoning map.\nL75: A zoning verification letter, which provides a summary of the zoning district, applicable standards, and zoning history for the property, is available upon request by submitting an application.\nL76:   * cite27†Zoning Regulations†cochisecounty.municipalcodeonline.com (link)\nL77:   * cite7†Interactive Zoning Map†cochise.maps.arcgis.com (link)\nL78:   * cite22†Zoning Verification Letter Application (PDF)\nL79: ### SUBDIVISIONS AND MINOR LAND DIVISIONS\nL80: \nL81: The County’s land division rules ensure orderly growth and adequate infrastructure such as access, roads, utilities, water, and wastewater systems. They also help ensure that structures are not built in areas subject to flooding and that parcel splits have accurate legal descriptions.\nL82: A subdivision is generally created when one parcel is divided into six (6) or more parcels, or when required by the Subdivision Regulations. Subdivisions are reviewed under the Cochise County Subdivision Regulations.\nL83: A minor land division is when one parcel is divided into five (5) or fewer parcels resulting in the creation of additional parcels, any of which are ten (10) acres or smaller. Minor land divisions are subject to administrative review by Planning staff. Staff will verify compliance with zoning regulations, confirm physical access, and ensure the split does not constitute a division of land subject to the Subdivision Regulations.\nL84:   * Subdivision Regulationscite28† (link)†cochisecounty.municipalcodeonline.com L85:   * Additional information about cite16†Subdividing Property†www.cochise.az.gov L86:   * Additional information about cite15†Minor Land Divisions†www.cochise.az.gov L87: ### COMPREHENSIVE/ LONG RANGE PLANNING\nL88: The Cochise County Comprehensive Plan (PDF) (cite29†link†www.cochise.az.gov ), adopted by the Board of Supervisors on March 10, 2026, is the County’s long-range planning document required under ARS §11-804 that guides growth and development through 2045. The plan establishes goals, policies, and land use guidance to support coordinated decisions related to land use, transportation, water resources, infrastructure, housing, and economic development.\nL89: It does not rezone property or approve specific projects, but provides the policy framework that informs future planning decisions while supporting responsible growth and preserving Cochise County’s rural character..\nL90: ### cite30†Contact Us L91: \nL92:   1. #### Matthew Taylor\nL93: \nL94: Planning Manager\nL95: \nL96: mtaylor@cochise.az.gov\nL97: \nL98: Phone: 520-432-9256\nL99: \nL100:   2. #### Development Services\nL101: \nL102: developmentservices@cochise.az.gov\nL103: \nL104: Physical Address\nL105: 1415 Melody Lane\nL106: Building F\nL107: Bisbee, AZ 85603\nL108: \nL109: Phone: 520-432-9300\nL110: ### How to Apply Online (Citizenserve Portal)\nL111: \nL112: Most planning requests can be submitted online through the cite8†Citizenserve portal (link). †www4.citizenserve.com L113:   1. Create an account. Once registered, applicants may apply for permits and applications, schedule inspections, and more.\nL114:   2. Complete the appropriate cite31†fillable PDF application (link).†www4.citizenserve.com L115:   3. Log in and click Apply Online.\nL116:   4. Select the Project Type (example: Minor Land Division) and Sub Type (example: 4-Lot), if applicable.\nL117:   5. Enter the Parcel Number (example format: 12345678A) and select “Find Address.”\nL118:   6. Upload the application and supporting materials and complete all required fields. Click Submit.\nL119: After acceptance, a member of the Planning staff will contact the applicant. If the application is complete, it will be placed “under review,” and staff will provide next steps.\nL120: \nL121:   * cite32†Agendas & Minutes L122: \nL123:   * cite33†Employment L124: \nL125:   * cite34†Pay Online L126: \nL127:   * cite35†Permits†www.citizenserve.com L128: \nL129:   * cite36†Notifications†public.alertsense.com L130: \nL131:   * cite37†Vital Records L132: \nL133:   1.   *   *   *   *   * ### Contact Us\nL134: \nL135:   1. County Offices\nL136: \nL137:   2. 1415 Melody Lane, Building G\nL138: \nL139:   3. Bisbee, AZ 85603\nL140: ### cite38†Quick Links L141: \nL142:   1. cite39†Arizona Department of Revenue Property Tax Forms†azdor.gov L143: \nL144:   2. cite40†State Historic Property Tax Reclassification (SPT) Owner-Occupied Homes†azstateparks.com L145: \nL146: ### cite41†Site Links L147: \nL148:   1. cite3†Home L149: \nL150:   2. cite42†Site Map L151: \nL152:   3. cite43†Accessibility L153: \nL154: Government Websites by cite44†CivicPlus®†connect.civicplus.com --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLayer: Cad_Parcel_TaxInfo (ID:0) (https://services6.arcgis.com/Yxem0VOcqSy8T6TE/arcgis/rest/services/Cad_Parcel_TaxInfo/FeatureServer/0)\nciteturn2view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://services6.arcgis.com/Yxem0VOcqSy8T6TE/arcgis/rest/services/Cad_Parcel_TaxInfo/FeatureServer/0\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 85\nL0: ArcGIS REST Services Directory\nL1: | cite0†API Reference†resources.arcgis.com L2: \nL3: cite1†JSON L4: ## Layer: Cad_Parcel_TaxInfo (ID:0)\nL5: \nL6: View In:   cite2†Map Viewer†www.arcgis.com L7: \nL8: Name: Cad_Parcel_TaxInfo\nL9: Display Field: owner_name1\nL10: Type: Feature Layer\nL11: Geometry Type: esriGeometryPolygon\nL12: Has Views: true\nL13: Source Schema Changes Allowed: true\nL14: cite3†Views L15: Description:\nL16: Copyright Text:\nL17: Min. Scale: 0\nL18: Max. Scale: 0\nL19: Default Visibility: true\nL20: Max Record Count: 2000\nL21: Supported query Formats: JSON, geoJSON, PBF\nL22: Use Standardized Queries: True\nL23: Extent:\nL24